        "text": "I have now reviewed every location where a restraint on our business could sit: the definitions (Field of Use), Article II's licence grant and Additional Restrictions, Articles III–VII, the Confidential Information/Non‑Solicitation article, the Change of Control/ROFR articles, and General Provisions.\n\nKey findings:\n- **p0007 / p0030**: \"Field of Use\" limits *how we may use Licensor's own Licensed Technology* (Spot FX market data and order transmission). It is a scope limitation on the grant, not a covenant about the businesses we may run or the products we may buy or build.\n- **p0027, p0033, p0040–p0047, p0085**: all restrictions are tied to the *Licensed Technology* (no distribution, no derivative works, no reverse engineering) — licence-integrity terms, not non-competes.\n- **p0043**: licence is expressly non‑exclusive and Licensor retains full rights to license others — no Vendor exclusivity over any product or brand of ours.\n- **p0125**: the only post-term covenant on us is an employee non‑solicit (a different rule); there is no post-term non-compete.\n- **p0134/p0139**: change-of-control consent and ROFR are assignment/exit mechanics (terminating the licence), not prohibitions on our operations, and belong to the assignment rules rather than being double-flagged here.\n\nNo provision restricts us from developing, acquiring, buying or operating competing FX platforms or products, and there is no territory restriction. Accordingly this sits at the preferred position and I will not redline it."
